---
source: src/main.rs
expression: "render_help_snapshot(&[\"anon\", \"tunnel\"])"
---
Expose a local HTTP server without signing in

Usage: hooklistener anon tunnel [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -p, --port <PORT>         Local port to forward requests to [default: 3000]
      --host <HOST>         Local host to forward to [default: localhost]
      --name <NAME>         Stable public route name
      --ttl <DURATION>      Route lifetime, such as 300, 10m, or 30m [default: 15m]
      --allow-non-loopback  Allow forwarding to a host that resolves outside loopback
  -h, --help                Print help

Global options:
      --json               Output supported command responses or event streams as JSON
      --color <COLOR>      Styling policy for human output [default: auto] [possible values: auto,
                           always, never]
      --yes                Confirm destructive commands without an interactive prompt
      --log-level <LEVEL>  Log level [default: info] [possible values: trace, debug, info, warn,
                           error]
      --log-dir <DIR>      Directory for log files
      --log-stdout         Also write logs to stdout
